==Trivia==
*Truth's Devouring Maw's Japanese name, Banbutsu Izanau Shinri no Ōuzu (万物誘う真理の大渦, "Great Whirlpool of Truth That Entices All Things"), may be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton|Isaac Newton]] quote "I do not know what I may appear to the world, but to myself I seem to have been only like a boy playing on the sea-shore, and diverting myself in now and then finding a smoother pebble or a prettier shell than ordinary, whilst the <u>great ocean of truth</u> lay all undiscovered before me."
**[[Newton's Fruit]] refers to the falling apple that inspired Newton's gravitational theory, while [[Divided Light]]'s Japanese name, Nanairo ni Wakatareru Hikari (七色に分かたれる光, "Light Divided into Seven Colors"), references Newton's contributions to [[wikipedia:Optics|optics]], in particular his famous experiment determining that a prism disperses white light into its constituent colors.
***Newton's theory of color superseded [[wikipedia:Aristotle|Aristotle]]'s theory that all colors are a mix of black and white, and Divided Light only contains [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and white enemies.
**Based on its Japanese name, [[Immeasurable Power]] may have been intended as a reference to [[wikipedia:Newton's laws of motion|Newton's laws of motion]], which revolve around force, or Newton's eponymous SI unit for measuring force, the [[wikipedia:Newton (unit)|newton]]. 力 was officially translated as "Power", but can also mean "force".
**Truth's Devouring Maw having a Newton-inspired boss and [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] may have been foreshadowed by the name of the sub-chapter preceding it, [[Newtown Trench]].
*Truth's Devouring Maw may have been inspired by Abrahamic religions' story of the [[wikipedia:Garden of Eden|Garden of Eden]], as it was added in the same update as [[Temptation's Rhapsody]], its Japanese name can be translated as "Great Whirlpool of Truth That <u>Tempts</u> All Things", Sage of Logic Newtone has an apple (the most common depiction of the [[wikipedia:Forbidden fruit|forbidden fruit]]), and eating the fruit gave Adam and Eve forbidden [[:Category:Sage  Enemies|knowledge]]. Furthermore, Immeasurable Power contains [[Angelic Gory]], a fallen [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], and the serpent that tempted Eve is often associated with [[wikipedia:Samael|Samael]] and Satan, who are fallen angels in many of their depictions.
*The whirlpool that represents Immeasurable Power can be seen earlier when viewing [[Permission to Land]], the first [[Zero Legends]] stage to take place in a [[Media:Map042.png|rearranged North and South America]].
*Immeasurable Power looks nearly identical to [[The Great Abyss (Into the Future)|The Great Abyss]] from [[Into the Future]]'s map.
*Truth's Devouring Maw is the last [[Zero Legends]] sub-chapter to take place in a cluttered and reshuffled version of North America and South America, the first being [[Stratospheric Pathway]].

